note Source: Node.js lib/events.js, _listeners (backs emitter.listeners and rawListeners).

note GAP: stored callbacks - listeners are JavaScript functions kept in a data structure and
note called later. The doc has no function type, so an invented `Listener` type stands for one.
note A `once` listener is a wrapper function with a `listener` property pointing at the user's
note original function; that is modelled as a choice instead of a property on a function.
choice Listener
    Plain with handler as a Handler
    Once_wrapper with wrapper as a Handler and listener as a Handler

note WORKAROUND: Node stores either one function or an array of functions under each event
note name, to save an array allocation in the common case. `typeof evlistener === 'function'`
note is a run-time type test; Scribe needs the two shapes as a declared choice.
choice EventSlot
    Single with entry as a Listener
    Many with entries as a List of Listener

note GAP: dynamic objects as maps - target._events is a prototype-less object used as a map
note from event name (a string or a Symbol) to an EventSlot, and it may be undefined. The doc has
note no map type and no Symbol type; an invented `Map of EventName to EventSlot` is used and
note lookup is written `lookup type in events`, returning a maybe.
note GAP: duck typing - _listeners accepts any target that has an _events property (any
note EventEmitter or subclass). There are no interfaces, so a concrete Emitter type is used.
type Emitter
    field events as a maybe Map of EventName to EventSlot

to lookup name in table
    given name is an EventName
    given table is a Map of EventName to EventSlot
    produces a maybe EventSlot

to handler_of entry
    given entry is a Listener
    produces a Handler

to unwrap_listeners entries using memory
    given entries is a List of Listener
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces a List of Handler
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

to array_clone entries using memory
    given entries is a List of Listener
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces a List of Handler
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

note WORKAROUND: `unwrap` is a plain JavaScript boolean flag; kept as a Bool parameter with a
note label word, since the doc has no keyword or optional arguments.
to listeners_of target for type unwrapped unwrap using memory
    given target is an Emitter
    given type is an EventName
    given unwrap is a Bool
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces a List of Handler
    fails with OutOfMemory
    uses memory

    note WORKAROUND: two `=== undefined` early returns become two nested `choose` blocks.
    choose events of target
        when nothing
            give back []
        when some events
            choose lookup type in events
                when nothing
                    give back []
                when some slot
                    choose slot
                        when Single with entry
                            note `evlistener.listener || evlistener`: when unwrapping, a once
                            note wrapper yields the user's original function.
                            if unwrap
                                choose entry
                                    when Once_wrapper with wrapper and listener
                                        give back [listener]
                                    when Plain with handler
                                        give back [handler]
                            give back [handler_of entry]
                        when Many with entries
                            if unwrap
                                give back try unwrap_listeners entries using memory
                            give back try array_clone entries using memory
